I'll read both files now.I need to read the rest of the findings file (lines 283-920).Based on my complete review of both files, I checked every concrete claim and citation. The section is very faithful overall—the vast majority of numbers, locations, and findings map correctly to the cited papers. I found one claim that contradicts its source.

The Pan2023 claim states moldboard tillage reduces drainage DRP/PP "but at the cost of higher runoff losses." However, the Pan2023 findings show the opposite for runoff P: "Under CMP75, conventional tillage caused a 50.04% decrease in overall P loss through runoff and an 18.58% decrease in overall P loss through tile drainage compared with no-till" (i.e., tillage reduced BOTH runoff and drainage P losses, not increased runoff losses).

